{{define "content"}}
<div class="config-sub" id="page-config-agent">
{{template "config_sub_header" $}}
<h1>Coding agent</h1>
<p class="sub">
  Which CLI runs a session, and on which model. The model name picks the CLI —
  <span class="mono">sonnet</span> runs Claude Code, <span class="mono">claude-opus-5-thinking-high</span> runs Cursor,
  <span class="mono">grok-4.6</span> runs Grok.
  These are the defaults; a builder may override the model per session when starting work in the web UI.
  A session stamps the agent and model it started on and keeps them for life, since a
  session cannot be resumed by the other CLI — so changes here only affect <strong>new</strong> sessions.
</p>

<div class="section card">
  <form method="post" action="{{route "config.agent"}}">
    {{template "csrf" $}}

    <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.35rem">Models</h2>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:0 0 0.65rem">
      A title run is one cheap tools-off turn, so it can use a smaller model or the other CLI.
      The review model is the default for sessions dispatched from a commit or pull request.
      Both blank fields fall back to the task model.
    </p>
    {{/* .inline bottom-aligns by default, which staggers these three labels as soon
         as one field's note wraps to a second line. */}}
    <div class="inline" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;align-items:start">
      <div>
        <label for="model">Task model</label>
        <select id="model" name="model" data-model-limits="model-limits">
          <option value=""{{if .Config.FallbackLimits}} data-limits="{{.Config.FallbackLimits}}"{{end}}>CLI default</option>
          {{template "model_optgroups" .Config.ModelGroups}}
        </select>
        <p class="sub" style="margin:0.35rem 0 0" id="model-agent">
          {{if .Config.Model}}
            {{if .Config.ModelAgentKnown}}→ runs on <strong>{{if eq .Config.ModelAgent "claude"}}Claude{{else if eq .Config.ModelAgent "cursor"}}Cursor{{else}}Grok{{end}}</strong>
            {{else}}→ name not recognized, using the fallback agent{{end}}
          {{else}}→ fallback agent, each CLI picks its own default model{{end}}
        </p>
        <p class="model-limits" id="model-limits"{{if not .Config.ModelLimits}} hidden{{end}}>{{.Config.ModelLimits}}</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="summarize-model">Session-title model</label>
        <select id="summarize-model" name="summarizeModel" data-model-limits="summarize-limits">
          <option value=""{{if .Config.ModelLimits}} data-limits="{{.Config.ModelLimits}}"{{end}}>Same as task model</option>
          {{template "model_optgroups" .Config.SummarizeModelGroups}}
        </select>
        <p class="sub" style="margin:0.35rem 0 0" id="summarize-agent">
          {{if .Config.SummarizeModel}}
            {{if .Config.SummarizeAgentKnown}}→ runs on <strong>{{if eq .Config.SummarizeAgent "claude"}}Claude{{else if eq .Config.SummarizeAgent "cursor"}}Cursor{{else}}Grok{{end}}</strong>
            {{else}}→ name not recognized, runs on the session's agent{{end}}
          {{else}}→ same as the task model{{end}}
        </p>
        <p class="model-limits" id="summarize-limits"{{if not .Config.SummarizeLimits}} hidden{{end}}>{{.Config.SummarizeLimits}}</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="review-model">Review model</label>
        <select id="review-model" name="reviewModel" data-model-limits="review-limits">
          <option value=""{{if .Config.ModelLimits}} data-limits="{{.Config.ModelLimits}}"{{end}}>Same as task model</option>
          {{template "model_optgroups" .Config.ReviewModelGroups}}
        </select>
        <p class="sub" style="margin:0.35rem 0 0" id="review-agent">
          {{if .Config.ReviewModel}}
            {{if .Config.ReviewAgentKnown}}→ runs on <strong>{{if eq .Config.ReviewAgent "claude"}}Claude{{else if eq .Config.ReviewAgent "cursor"}}Cursor{{else}}Grok{{end}}</strong>
            {{else}}→ name not recognized, using the fallback agent{{end}}
          {{else}}→ same as the task model{{end}}
        </p>
        <p class="model-limits" id="review-limits"{{if not .Config.ReviewLimits}} hidden{{end}}>{{.Config.ReviewLimits}}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:1.25rem 0 0.35rem">Binaries &amp; fallback</h2>
    <div class="inline" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;">
      <div>
        <label for="agent">Fallback agent</label>
        <select id="agent" name="agent">
          <option value="grok" {{if eq .Config.Agent "grok"}}selected{{end}}>Grok</option>
          <option value="claude" {{if eq .Config.Agent "claude"}}selected{{end}}>Claude</option>
          <option value="cursor" {{if eq .Config.Agent "cursor"}}selected{{end}}>Cursor</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="grok-bin">Grok binary</label>
        <input id="grok-bin" type="text" name="grokBin" value="{{.Config.GrokBin}}" placeholder="grok" autocomplete="off">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="claude-bin">Claude binary</label>
        <input id="claude-bin" type="text" name="claudeBin" value="{{.Config.ClaudeBin}}" placeholder="claude" autocomplete="off">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="cursor-bin">Cursor binary</label>
        <input id="cursor-bin" type="text" name="cursorBin" value="{{.Config.CursorBin}}" placeholder="cursor-agent" autocomplete="off">
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:0.5rem 0 0">
      The fallback agent is used when the model field is blank or its name identifies neither CLI.
      An unrecognized name is passed through unchanged, so the CLI reports it.
    </p>

    {{/* .switch is an icon-only control (fixed 2.9rem box, knob absolutely
         covering it), so its text label sits beside it, not inside. */}}
    <div class="section" style="margin-top:1rem;display:flex;gap:0.75rem;align-items:start">
      <label class="switch" title="Pass ANTHROPIC_* to claude runs" style="flex:none;margin-top:0.1rem">
        <input type="checkbox" name="claudeIncludeAnthropicEnv" value="1" {{if .Config.ClaudeIncludeAnthropicEnv}}checked{{end}}>
        <span class="knob" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="sr-only">Pass ANTHROPIC_* to claude runs</span>
      </label>
      <div>
        <strong>Pass <span class="mono">ANTHROPIC_*</span> to claude runs</strong>
        <p class="sub" style="margin:0.35rem 0 0">
          Off by default: host credentials are stripped from every agent child, and a normal
          OAuth login authenticates from the keychain without any environment variable.
          Turn this on only for API-key, gateway, or custom base-URL setups — it hands the
          agent process your Anthropic credentials.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:1rem"><button type="submit">Save</button></div>
  </form>
</div>
</div>
{{end}}
